s=json.loads(Path(sys.argv[1]).read_text());out=Path(sys.argv[2]);p=s['primary'];before=p['medians']['before'];after=p['medians']['after'];comparison=p['comparisons']['after_over_before'];families=s['allocation_comparison']
lines=['# R64: first-only central projection budget checks','',f"Candidate build: `{s['static']['after']['source']}`. Baseline R63 build: `{s['static']['before']['source']}`. Accepted baseline checkpoint: `{s['baseline_provenance']['accepted_checkpoint']}`.",'',f"The complete eight-byte level-12 call measured **{after['multiple_of_reference']:.6f}× the reference**, from **{before['multiple_of_reference']:.6f}×** in this matched baseline cohort. Candidate/baseline elapsed: **{comparison['pooled_ratio']:.8f}×** ({s['changes_percent']['primary_seconds']:+.4f}%). The freshly measured reference median was {p['reference_seconds']*1000:.6f} ms.",'','Two central projection-meter queries use the existing first-violation evaluator instead of constructing the full list of violations. Both APIs traverse the same ordered Core checks. Preview still checks arithmetic, worker-scope restrictions, scope authorization and enclosing-work funding before call policy. Charge retains its current enclosing-work prefix before policy rejection, leaves accumulated meter state unchanged on failure, and commits only after all checks pass. The new tests exercise competing policy and funding failures, compute/node overflow, unchanged state and retry on both parent and candidate.','', 'Engine, Compute, Stdlib, Runtime and GPU were rebuilt coherently with their retained flags/features and warnings-as-errors. Core, math, syntax and external artifacts remain frozen. The candidate emits its Object, descriptor and metadata afresh; all three must match the R63 baseline byte-for-byte. No compressor source, algorithm, source allocation site or timing boundary changes.','', '| Metric | Reference | R63 baseline | R64 candidate | Change |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|',f"| Primary elapsed (ms) | {p['reference_seconds']*1000:.6f} | {before['seconds']*1000:.6f} | {after['seconds']*1000:.6f} | {s['changes_percent']['primary_seconds']:+.4f}% |"]
for section,key,label in [('cpu','instructions','Retired instructions'),('cpu','cycles','CPU cycles'),('allocation','allocation_requests','Allocation requests'),('allocation','requested_bytes','Requested bytes'),('allocation','reallocations','Reallocations'),('allocation','peak_live_usable','Peak allocator live usable bytes'),('allocation','incremental_peak_live_usable','Incremental allocator peak'),('cpu','rss_after','RSS after call'),('cpu','physical_after','Physical footprint after call')]:
 values=[s[section][variant][key]['median'] for variant in ['reference','before','after']];change=s['changes_percent'][key]
 lines.append('| '+label+' | '+' | '.join(f'{v:,.1f}' if int(v)!=v else f'{v:,.0f}' for v in values)+' | '+('—' if change is None else f'{change:+.4f}%')+' |')
lines+=['','Primary elapsed, CPU counters, heap counters and CPU-time samples are separate serial cohorts. Their percentages are not multiplied or combined. Requested bytes represent allocation requests, not initialized bytes copied. Allocator peak and post-call OS footprint are different measures; the latter is not peak RSS and includes retained compiler/catalog/image storage.','', '## Allocation and instruction mechanism','', 'The successful full-budget evaluator already returns an allocation-free empty vector. This change predicts zero successful-call allocation savings; it targets the work around the existing call boundary. Failure-only savings cannot explain successful primary elapsed. Hardware instruction changes are measured independently of allocator counts and CPU-time samples.','', '| Complete census | R63 baseline | R64 candidate | Delta |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
for key,label in [('requests','Allocation requests'),('requested_bytes','Requested bytes'),('reallocations','Reallocations')]:
 lines.append(f"| {label} | {families['before'][key]:,} | {families['after'][key]:,} | {families['whole_call_delta'][key]:+,} |")
lines+=['',f"Size/kind request histogram unchanged: **{families['size_kind_histogram_unchanged']}**. Both full censuses are fresh R64 measurements, individually reconciled to their separate eight-observation heap cohorts. The archived trace pins and per-size counts are in `allocation-comparison.json`. Equal totals do not establish identical work or execution counts.",'', 'A retained R62 CPU sample attributed 19 of 1,320 exclusive sample weights to the full budget evaluator. That was a lead for this experiment, not a predicted elapsed or instruction saving and not an R64 observation. Fresh whole-call counters and samples are the result evidence.','', '## Matched pairs and adverse observations','', '| Pair | Baseline ms | Candidate ms | Candidate/baseline |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
for group in p['groups']:lines.append(f"| {group['group']} | {group['medians']['before']*1000:.6f} | {group['medians']['after']*1000:.6f} | {group['after_over_before']:.8f}× |")
lines+=['',f"{comparison['improving_groups']}/4 independently prepared pairs and {comparison['improving_blocks']}/64 alternating blocks improved. Four pairs ×16 blocks ×31 calls ×2 variants produce 3,968 timed observations. Blocks within one pair are descriptive, not independent repetitions."]
adverse=s['contrary_primary_groups']
lines.append('Adverse or unchanged primary pairs: '+(', '.join(str(x['group'])+f" ({100*(x['after_over_before']-1):+.4f}%)" for x in adverse) if adverse else 'none.'))
d=s['diagnostic_cpu_elapsed'];lines+=['',f"The separate CPU-counter cohort elapsed was {d['before']['median_seconds']*1000:.6f} → {d['after']['median_seconds']*1000:.6f} ms ({d['change_percent']:+.6f}%). These 32 observations per variant are excluded from primary elapsed and retain their independent direction.",'','Other observed median increases:','','```json',json.dumps(s['contrary_counter_directions'],indent=2),'```','', '## Binary and baseline provenance','', '| Metric | R63 baseline | R64 candidate |','|---|---:|---:|']
for key,label in [('code_bytes','Generated text bytes'),('stack_bytes','Machine entry stack bytes'),('typed_ir_version','Typed IR version'),('abi_version','ABI version')]:lines.append(f"| {label} | {s['static']['before'][key]:,} | {s['static']['after'][key]:,} |")
lines+=['','Object/image/metadata equality: '+str(all(s['artifact_pin_equality'].values()))+'. The unchanged generated bytes have unchanged static instruction content. Hardware retired instructions can still change because this patch changes host admission work. `binary-audit.json` records each actual image pin.', '', s['baseline_provenance']['source_note'],'',s['baseline_provenance']['binary_note'],'', 'These historical notes preserve provenance; no R63 measurement or test execution is counted as an R64 observation.','', '## Workload and correctness','', 'Input: eight bytes `abcdefgh`. Exact raw output: `[75,76,74,78,73,77,75,207,0,0]`, independently inflated. Output capacity 13 is cleared/reused. The tree has 262,144 U16 entries; the cache has 1,500,513 U32 words; depth is 300 and nice length 258. Original source allocation sites, input aliases and allocator are retained. Logical work is 60,260,219,686 and comparison work is 47,612; neither is a hardware instruction count. Successful invocations finish with zero managed bytes/nodes.','', '```json',json.dumps(s['source_pins'],indent=2),'```','', '## Qualification','',f"Status: **{s['validation']['status']}**. Counts below are actual executed receipts; inventory-only rows are omitted from this view and remain in `validation.json`. Batches overlap.",'', '| Receipt | Expected tests | Observed | Exit / expected | Passed |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---|']
for row in s['validation']['checks']:
 if row.get('inventory_only'):continue
 lines.append(f"| `{row['receipt']}` | {row.get('expected_tests','—')} | {row.get('observed_tests',row.get('cases','—'))} | {row.get('exit','—')} / {row.get('expected_exit',0)} | {row['passed']} |")
lines+=['',s['validation']['parent_candidate_scope'],'',s['validation']['runtime_coverage']['scope'],'','The local `ci.py` Engine batches execute all 12 projection-meter tests and all six inherited frame-shape tests using the retained broader Engine test feature configuration. Core also executes its two existing first-violation equivalence/order tests. The complete commands are archived; this is not a claim that the local Engine build used exactly a minimal CI feature set or that remote CI completed.','', 'Earlier failed attempts and dispositions:']
